A feature that could make QueueLess unique

One differentiator would be a "Leave the Queue Without Losing Your Spot" feature.

Imagine you're waiting in a hospital queue. The app could allow you to step out briefly (for example, to get food or use the restroom) while tracking your location. If you move too far away, it warns you before your turn arrives. If you're nearby, it reminds you to return just in time. This gives users more flexibility while helping businesses reduce missed turns.

That kind of intelligent queue management is less common than basic digital ticketing and could help QueueLess stand out.

Overall, I'd recommend focusing first on a polished MVP with digital queues, live tracking, notifications, an admin dashboard, and queue analytics. Once those work reliably, you can add AI wait-time predictions, QR check-in, and the unique "leave without losing your spot" capability.